<!--
  Document-structure layer for the proof of concept.
  USLM-aligned markup of DoD Instruction 1327.06, conforming to the USMC
  issuance schema (schema/usmc-issuance-1.0.xsd).

  The current edition (Effective August 7, 2025, "Military Leave, Liberty, and
  Administrative Absence") reissues and cancels the June 16, 2009 edition
  ("Leave and Liberty Policy and Procedures") that MARADMIN 051/23 and DTM 23-001
  cite by number; DTM 23-001 was to be incorporated into this instruction.

  SCOPE: the Purpose is encoded in full, and the complete Section/paragraph
  structure is encoded from the table of contents (headings are verbatim; status
  VERIFIED as to their existence and titles). Section and paragraph BODIES are
  large and NOT yet encoded, except as stated below. The current parental-leave
  procedures live at 3.11.c (ADPL) and 3.11.d (IDPL).

  DEEPENING, 2026-08-08: selected paragraph bodies under 3.11.c and 3.11.d are
  now encoded from the Change 1 edition (DoWI 1327.06, August 7, 2025,
  incorporating Change 1, June 30, 2026; sha256:1718797f...; full artifact
  record in data/dodi-1327.06.rules.json). The skeleton above and around them
  remains encoded from the base August 7, 2025 edition's table of contents -
  the two editions' 3.11 structure is identical for the paragraphs encoded
  here, per the corrections record in data/dodi-1327.06.rules.json. The
  transcriptions were machine-read from that PDF and carried here via the
  verbatim quotes recorded in data/dodi-1327.06.rules.json and
  verification/findings-dodi-1327.06.md, so every deepened node is UNVERIFIED
  until a human attests it. Where only part of a paragraph's text was
  transcribed, the node says so in an adjacent comment; sibling paragraphs that
  exist in the source but are not transcribed are a stated gap, not an
  omission by accident.
-->
