    <paragraph identifier="/us/dod/dodi/1327.06/s3/3.11" status="VERIFIED">
      <num style="compound">3.11</num><heading>Non-chargeable Leave</heading>
      <paragraph identifier="/us/dod/dodi/1327.06/s3/3.11/a" status="VERIFIED"><num style="alpha-lower">a</num><heading>Convalescent Leave</heading></paragraph>
      <paragraph identifier="/us/dod/dodi/1327.06/s3/3.11/b" status="VERIFIED"><num style="alpha-lower">b</num><heading>RC Maternity Leave</heading></paragraph>
      <paragraph identifier="/us/dod/dodi/1327.06/s3/3.11/c" status="VERIFIED">
        <num style="alpha-lower">c</num>
        <heading>ADPL (Active Duty Parental Leave)</heading>
        <paragraph identifier="/us/dod/dodi/1327.06/s3/3.11/c/adpl-entitlement" status="UNVERIFIED">
          <content><p>Retired editorial anchor. This identifier was the citation target for the 12-week ADPL entitlement before the paragraph bodies below were encoded; the entitlement is stated in the source at 3.11.c.(3)(a)1, now encoded below. The identifier is kept because it was allocated and cited; nothing should cite it going forward.</p></content>
        </paragraph>
        <!-- (1), (2) exist in the source; not transcribed. -->
        <paragraph identifier="/us/dod/dodi/1327.06/s3/3.11/c/3" status="UNVERIFIED">
          <num style="paren-arabic">(3)</num>
          <paragraph identifier="/us/dod/dodi/1327.06/s3/3.11/c/3/a" status="UNVERIFIED">
            <num style="paren-alpha">(a)</num>
            <content><p>For the birth parent, 12 weeks of ADPL is authorized following a period of convalescence from childbirth.</p></content>
            <paragraph identifier="/us/dod/dodi/1327.06/s3/3.11/c/3/a/1" status="UNVERIFIED">
              <num style="arabic">1</num>
              <content><p>Twelve weeks of ADPL is authorized during the 1-year period beginning after the child's date of birth.</p></content>
            </paragraph>
          </paragraph>
          <paragraph identifier="/us/dod/dodi/1327.06/s3/3.11/c/3/b" status="UNVERIFIED">
            <num style="paren-alpha">(b)</num>
            <content><p>For the non-birth parent, 12 weeks of ADPL is authorized during the 1-year period beginning after the child's date of birth.</p></content>
          </paragraph>
        </paragraph>
        <!-- (4), (5) state the same 12 weeks for adoption and long-term foster
             care; their transcriptions in verification/findings-dodi-1327.06.md
             are truncated, so they are not encoded yet. -->
        <paragraph identifier="/us/dod/dodi/1327.06/s3/3.11/c/6" status="UNVERIFIED">
          <num style="paren-arabic">(6)</num>
          <!-- (a) states the converse (events outside the 72-hour period are
               separate events); not transcribed. -->
          <paragraph identifier="/us/dod/dodi/1327.06/s3/3.11/c/6/b" status="UNVERIFIED">
            <num style="paren-alpha">(b)</num>
            <content><p>Multiple qualifying events occurring within the same 72-hour period will be treated as a single event for the allocation of ADPL.</p></content>
          </paragraph>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph identifier="/us/dod/dodi/1327.06/s3/3.11/c/7" status="UNVERIFIED">
          <num style="paren-arabic">(7)</num>
          <paragraph identifier="/us/dod/dodi/1327.06/s3/3.11/c/7/a" status="UNVERIFIED">
            <num style="paren-alpha">(a)</num>
            <!-- Excerpt: the sentence continues in the source; the remainder is
                 not transcribed. -->
            <content><p>Service members choosing to take ADPL in multiple increments must request such proposed leave in blocks of at least 7 days each for a maximum of 12 increments</p></content>
          </paragraph>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph identifier="/us/dod/dodi/1327.06/s3/3.11/c/10" status="UNVERIFIED">
          <num style="paren-arabic">(10)</num>
          <paragraph identifier="/us/dod/dodi/1327.06/s3/3.11/c/10/c" status="UNVERIFIED">
            <num style="paren-alpha">(c)</num>
            <content><p>ADPL that is not taken before the expiration of 1 year from the date of a child's birth, minor child's adoption by the Service member, or minor child's placement with the Service member for adoption or long-term foster care will be forfeited, unless Paragraph 3.11.c.(11) applies.</p></content>
          </paragraph>
        </paragraph>
        <!-- (11), the Change 1 two-year extension for a qualifying circumstance
             with first GO/FO approval, exists only in Change 1; not transcribed. -->
      </paragraph>
      <paragraph identifier="/us/dod/dodi/1327.06/s3/3.11/d" status="VERIFIED">
        <num style="alpha-lower">d</num>
        <heading>IDPL (Inactive Duty Parental Leave)</heading>
        <paragraph identifier="/us/dod/dodi/1327.06/s3/3.11/d/1" status="UNVERIFIED">
          <num style="paren-arabic">(1)</num>
          <paragraph identifier="/us/dod/dodi/1327.06/s3/3.11/d/1/c" status="UNVERIFIED">
            <num style="paren-alpha">(c)</num>
            <content><p>IDPL will be taken in increments equivalent to a 4-hour inactive duty training period of which a maximum of two such increments may be taken per day. Each such 4-hour increment constitutes an IDPL period.</p></content>
          </paragraph>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph identifier="/us/dod/dodi/1327.06/s3/3.11/d/3" status="UNVERIFIED">
          <num style="paren-arabic">(3)</num>
          <paragraph identifier="/us/dod/dodi/1327.06/s3/3.11/d/3/a" status="UNVERIFIED">
            <num style="paren-alpha">(a)</num>
            <!-- Excerpt: Change 1 wording ("Birth parent, ..."; the base edition
                 reads "For the birth parent"). The sentence continues in the
                 source; the remainder is not transcribed. -->
            <content><p>Birth parent, 12 IDPL periods will be authorized during the 1-year period</p></content>
          </paragraph>
        </paragraph>
      </paragraph>
